  "provenance": "V008 user annotated IMG_9112/IMG_9114: side relief moved to front Y0..20 Z60..80 while rear spine stays intact. Two independently adjustable, vertical symmetric rail/support-arm X pitches. M3 x 6-8 fasteners; parametric counterbore/head, floor wall and radial wall. Slimmer rails and rear contour. Actual PCB and connector geometry unmeasured. V009 corrects through-thickness port relief notches that crossed the M3 screw centerlines; retain a continuous central rail spine and integrated screw-bearing pads, with rear-open counterbores. V009 structural correction: no separate carrier. Both arms directly carry the M3 head seats, Ø3.4 through-bores, and rear Ø7 tool corridors; remaining front seat wall 3.2 mm. Provisional stations S=20/65 avoid front opening while measured PCB pattern remains unknown. V010: nominal Ø12 front neck around Ø7 rear driver access, X width tapered into the full structural arm; top excess trimmed to 9.5 mm above upper M3; analytic tangent arcs on the structural outer profile and a 1 mm keeper vertical-edge fillet. Critical bores, mating planes, source rail geometry and floor unchanged; print strength remains unqualified.",
